      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, I think you might have a typo in there—you said lower pH enhances the browning rate, but I thought alkaline environments usually accelerated it because they keep the amino groups in their reactive, unprotonated state. Could you double-check that and maybe explain the molecular mechanism of how the protonation state of the amino group specifically dictates the reaction speed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
